hexstrike-ai — https://github.com/0x4m4/hexstrike-ai  (MIT License)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

VIGIL reuses hexstrike-ai's deterministic DECISION MODEL (target profiling, tool-
effectiveness heuristics, per-tool parameter optimization, and named attack-pattern
playbooks) as the reasoning core of a pluggable agent body. This is a CLEAN-ROOM
reimplementation in integration/vigil_integration/brains/hexstrike_brain.py (design
credit + upstream line references in the module header), CURATED to recon/assessment
and DRIFT-FREE by construction — the upstream's evasion/stealth, credential-poisoning
(responder LLMNR/WPAD), WAF-tamper, and live-exploit/persistence stages are omitted.
The reimplementation is PROPOSE-ONLY: it emits proposed tools/params/chains as LEADs;
every proposal crosses VIGIL's conjunctive gate + egress gate and is executed only via
the gated external-tool runner, and a finding is minted a FACT only by a deterministic
VIGIL oracle.

The upstream hexstrike_server.py / hexstrike_mcp.py (a full offensive-execution
framework) are vendored under vendor/hexstrike-ai/ ONLY as non-runnable ".reference"
blobs — never imported, never executed, never on PYTHONPATH (see vendor/hexstrike-ai/
UPSTREAM.md; pinned commit d689933ff579d839c676c82b231f8e98326c5f04). The MIT LICENSE
is retained verbatim in that directory.

